{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 299,
    "dDurationMs": 1411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Dear Mr. President,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1710,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Do you know much about physics?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2710,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, you're the President of the United\nStates: a country with five thousand nuclear"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6730,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "weapons, birthplace of the world's computing\nand telecommunications industry, home of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10570,
    "dDurationMs": 3350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "first atomic clock and creator of the global\npositioning system."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13920,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But chances are, if you just took regular\nAmerican high school physics, you don't know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17600,
    "dDurationMs": 3589,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one iota about the science behind these things\n(No offense)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21189,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because high school physics students\nacross most of America are not required to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24289,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "learn about pretty much any physical phenomena\ndiscovered or explained more recently than"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27949,
    "dDurationMs": 1420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "1865."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29369,
    "dDurationMs": 2851,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes, 1865."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32220,
    "dDurationMs": 4010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's the year the civil war ended and well\nover a decade before Albert Einstein was even"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36230,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "born!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37230,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know what can happen in 150 years, Mr.\nPresident?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39120,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A lot."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40160,
    "dDurationMs": 1210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Velcro, for one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41370,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But let me list some useful and important\nideas of the last 150 years of physics that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44570,
    "dDurationMs": 3590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "aren't a required part of most standard US\nhigh school physics courses:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48160,
    "dDurationMs": 1010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Photons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49170,
    "dDurationMs": 1240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The structure of atoms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50410,
    "dDurationMs": 1429,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The existence of Antimatter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51839,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "GPS."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52839,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lasers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53839,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Transistors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54839,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Diodes and LEDs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55839,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Quarks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56839,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Chaos Theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57839,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Electron Microscopy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58839,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "MRI scanning."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59839,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Big Bang."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60839,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Black Holes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61839,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Star formation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62839,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The fact that gravity bends light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63839,
    "dDurationMs": 1031,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The fact that the universe is expanding."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64870,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Higgs Boson and the weak and strong nuclear\nforces and all the rest of quantum mechanics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68410,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and relativity and the topic of every single\nNobel Prize in Physics since…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72090,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "always."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73090,
    "dDurationMs": 1930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Basically, most of the important stuff."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75020,
    "dDurationMs": 4070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, Mr. President, imagine if history\nclasses didn't talk about the abolition of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79090,
    "dDurationMs": 4390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "slavery, world wars I or II, the great depression,\nthe rise of the US as a global superpower,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83480,
    "dDurationMs": 3970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the cold war or the civil rights movement\nor heaven forbid the first African American"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87450,
    "dDurationMs": 1010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "President."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88460,
    "dDurationMs": 4490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or imagine if biology classes didn't talk\nabout DNA, or hormones, or cell reproduction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92950,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or the modern germ theory of disease or ecology."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95790,
    "dDurationMs": 2990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or if geologists didn't talk about plate tectonics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98780,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And computer scientists…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99800,
    "dDurationMs": 4710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well… in 1865 a computer was a person who\ncomputed your taxes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104510,
    "dDurationMs": 4270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, if you were lucky enough to have an ambitious\nteacher or take Advanced Placement Physics,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108780,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then you might have learned about some of\nEinstein's discoveries of 1905!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111960,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112960,
    "dDurationMs": 1070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Current events!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114030,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But learning about how Einstein's work helped\nset the stage for a century of amazing developments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117590,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in our understanding of the universe is not\na part of the standard curriculum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121310,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So why, Mr. President, am I addressing this\nletter to you?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124760,
    "dDurationMs": 4190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, you appoint the Secretary of Education,\nfor one - and I do believe that high school"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128950,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "physics is somewhat related to education."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 131380,
    "dDurationMs": 4190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, maybe your education secretary says,\n\"ancient physics is already hard to teach"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135570,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to high schoolers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136570,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you want us to teach them modern physics\nwhich is even harder?!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139850,
    "dDurationMs": 3340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Students can't really appreciate the beauty\nof modern physics without fancy college level"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143190,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mathematics.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144190,
    "dDurationMs": 1130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "RUBBISH."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145320,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ever heard of Carl Sagan?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 146680,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Richard Feynman?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147680,
    "dDurationMs": 1570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or Neil deGrasse Tyson?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149250,
    "dDurationMs": 3710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These great men have been 100% committed to\nthe appreciation and dissemination of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152960,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "awesomeness of the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154620,
    "dDurationMs": 1370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we should be too."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 155990,
    "dDurationMs": 3550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How else are we supposed to foster and find\nour future brilliant innovators, inventors,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159540,
    "dDurationMs": 1070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and explorers?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160610,
    "dDurationMs": 3910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How can we expect to educate our citizens\nfor the next century if we don't teach about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164520,
    "dDurationMs": 1130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the last?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 165650,
    "dDurationMs": 3310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's not to say that we should ignore\nmath, either - on the contrary, math is one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168960,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the most beautiful and awesome things in\nthe universe, especially because it allows"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172580,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "us to understand the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174380,
    "dDurationMs": 4420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In particular, the last 150 years have borne\nfruit to perhaps the most drastic changes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178800,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in our understanding of the universe, ever,\nand these new ways of thinking and solving"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182400,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "problems should be the centerpiece of an education\nin physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186000,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Between you and me, Mr. President, I think\nwe'd better start making physics education"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189480,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more awesome here in the US, otherwise the\nnext Carl Sagan or Richard Feynman will come"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193890,
    "dDurationMs": 5460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from somewhere with more educational foresight\n- maybe even, the Internet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199350,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sincerely,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200350,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A collection of atoms known as Henry"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202240,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ps you're probably super busy, but if you'd\nlike to hear about physics education across"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205880,
    "dDurationMs": 4469,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Atlantic, I highly recommend heading over\nto Brady's channel, Sixty Symbols, for a perspective"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210349,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the UK."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211349,
    "dDurationMs": 13321,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I bet you'll enjoy it."
    } ]
  } ]
}
